    "date": "2026-11-14",
    "verdict": "approved",
    "note": "APPROVE after one re-review. First pass returned REQUEST CHANGES on one MAJOR, six MINORs and five NITs, all resolved. MAJOR: duplicate metadata keys supplied across separate @{ } blocks were silently accepted because the seen-bitmask was block-local; AfElement now holds a persistent meta_seen mask so in-block and cross-block duplicates reject uniformly. MINORs: the C++ frontmatter gate and the renderer-free generator now mirror parse_envelope (no-colon column-0 line rejects, # comments exempt, key trimmed before comparison); an implicit dedent can no longer close a container without an explicit end; connector/flow require non-empty labels; edges may not terminate at a connector (only connectorRef binds it); metadata comma splitting is quote-aware and %%{init}%% directives reject instead of being skipped as comments; fail-closed coverage was expanded to 30+ cases; shape metadata is node-only so it is never stored and silently dropped on a container. NITs closed: no-trailing-newline fence boundary, a local kSourceLimit guard, a duplicate row cap removed, and a write-only order field deleted. Independent probes measured the true 27 drawn / 11 config-gated / 0 error partition (19 draw at 40 columns, 8 fall back), 39/39 adversarial cases behave as intended, ASan cohort 4/4 with zero reports, and neighboring families are unaffected."
  },
